ic bling and nice  understated gold plating then there was  the fact that the entire campaign was  designed for you to play with a friend  which wasn't something I'd seen much of  before army of chair designed Corp in an  engaging way and was probably the first  shooter to make me realize how enormous  Lee fun upgrading your weapons and  mowing down baddies without really  caring about who they were or why you  were shooting at them could be I'd be  seriously remiss not to talk about the  game specifically designed to be played  by multiple people so let's talk about  what's so great about left 4 dead 2 not  only does it cleverly include two  numbers in the name the fact that the  survival horror shooter has been built  around your group means cop isn't just  encouraged it's vital you're one of the  few survivors of the zombie apocalypse  facing off against the Boomers and which  is to make your way through five  campaigns said campaigns alluded with  baddies safe houses and levels with  dynamic elements generated through the  game's AI director there are a variety  of both ranged and melee weapons to  choose from and it's a matter of playing  to your strengths as well as working  together with your team to survive the  game can get tricky especially if you  opted for realism mode which removes  respawns among other helpful gamey  features but if you've got three friends  handy there are certainly worse ways to  spend an evening  this one isn't your typical cop campaign  but it is still valve so since we're on  the topic let's talk portal to two  friends or two randoms on the internet  embody the testing robots atlas and  p-body each has a portal gun of their  own but both must work together to  complete a lengthy series of test  chambers after which they're brutally  ripped apart only to be reassembled  ready to go at the next chamber  this form of co-op is particularly  clever in how it demands that the  players work together sure the robot  buddies can high-five 